# Theme Scaffold Conventions

## 1. Folder Structure

- `templates/` for block templates
- `parts/` for template parts (no subfolders)
- `patterns/` for block patterns (PHP or JSON)
- `styles/` for style variation JSON files
- `assets/` for source JS/SCSS/images/fonts
- `inc/` for extra PHP includes
- `tests/` for Jest and Playwright tests
- `bin/` for scripts

## 2. File Naming

- Use `kebab-case` for slugs, lowercase for most files.
- Use `.mustache` for all files with placeholders.
- Use YAML front matter for Copilot/automation.

## 3. Placeholders

- All variable fields must be defined in [placeholder-schema-and-usage.md](./placeholder-schema-and-usage.md).
- Document all new uses.

## 4. Coding Standards

- Follow WordPress Coding Standards for PHP, JS, CSS/SCSS.
- Use automated linters/formatters.

## 5. Adding Files

- Add a front matter block to all new files for Copilot.
- Update all relevant docs and mapping schemas.

